No firmware
-----------
No Elektron firmware, and nothing extracted from it, is in this repository:
no .syx, no sections, no disassembly listings or code blocks copied from the
image (a detour re-emits the one or two instructions it displaces, written as
assembly source, as any patch must). You supply
your own stock OS file (stock/SHA256SUMS names the one the build is pinned to);
every build starts from it. Addresses in re/ and mods/ document where a patch
goes in that image; they are facts about it, not part of it. The registry's
guards hold the stock bytes they expect only as length + SHA-256, and a patch
that copies a stock record names its address (replace_from): the build reads
both from your image (tools/hash_expect.py).

Mods 0002-euclid-accents and 0003-velocity-humanise (older experiments, not in
any Sidecar release) are not published: 0002's accent icons were made from the
stock glyph bitmaps.

